request.description:
Purpose: List all system users (citizen, employee, and admin). Optional filters: search, role (`citizen`, `employee`, `admin`), department_id, is_active, page, and per_page (maximum 100).
Required role: admin
Required token: {{admin_token}}

Purpose: Provision an employee. An employee requires an existing active department. Passwords are accepted but never returned.
Required role: admin
Required token: {{admin_token}}

Purpose: Provision a system-wide admin. Admins do not have a department assignment.
Required role: admin
Required token: {{admin_token}}

Purpose: Provision a citizen without a department. This does not replace public citizen registration at `POST /auth/register`, which always creates a citizen.
Required role: admin
Required token: {{admin_token}}

Purpose: Show the safe UserResource representation: id, name, email, phone, national_id, role, department, is_active, phone_verified_at, and last_login_at. Passwords, OTP data, and Sanctum token hashes are never returned.
Required role: admin
Required token: {{admin_token}}

Purpose: Update safe profile, role, or department fields. Use this body for an existing employee department update. Employees require an active department; citizens and admins have their department cleared. Do NOT send is_active here: it returns 422. Use Update User Status instead. An admin cannot demote their own role.
Required role: admin
Required token: {{admin_token}}

Purpose: Deactivate a user. Set is_active to true to reactivate. Deactivation revokes every Sanctum token; reactivation does not restore old tokens, so the user must authenticate again. An admin cannot deactivate themselves, and the final active admin cannot be deactivated.
Required role: admin
Required token: {{admin_token}}

Negative validation example. This request must return 422 because account status is only changed by `PATCH /admin/users/{user}/status`. Run manually; it is not part of a happy-path sequence.
Required role: admin
Required token: {{admin_token}}

